<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n330" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">accentus</span></b> , ūs, m.
		accino, the attuning a thing; hence
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen., <i>a
				blast</i>, <i>signal</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aeneatorum accentu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 16, 12, 36</span></i>
			: <i><span class="en">id. 24, 4, 22</span></i>; acutissimi
			tibiarum, Solin. 5 <i>fin.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			gramm., <i>the accentuation of a word</i>, <i>accent</i>, <i>tone</i> (post-Aug.):
			accentus, quos Graeci <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσωδίας</span>
			vocant (so that it is a lit. transl. of the Gr. word, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός</span> = ad, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾠδή</span> = cantus), <i><span class="en">Quint. 1,
				5, 22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12,
				10, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Diom. p. 425</span></i>
			Putsch.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Fig.,
				<i>intensity</i>, <i>violence</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hiemis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">doloris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Marc. Emp. 36</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
